#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:302
msgid "open this to show some further options; don't bother with this unless you have a problem or are curious."
msgstr "abre esto para mostrar algunas opciones adicionales; no te molestes con esto a menos que tengas un problema o sientas curiosidad."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:312
msgid "Debug mode"
msgstr "Modo de depuración"

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:313
msgid "Check this to receive more information and emails on the backup process - useful if something is going wrong."
msgstr "Marca esta opción para recibir más información y correos sobre el proceso de respaldo; es útil si algo está fallando."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:313
msgid "This will also cause debugging output from all plugins to be shown upon this screen - please do not be surprised to see these."
msgstr "Esto también hará que se muestre en esta pantalla la salida de depuración de todos los plugins; no te sorprendas si aparecen."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:317
msgid "Split archives every:"
msgstr "Dividir archivos cada:"

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:321
msgid "BackupPlus will split up backup archives when they exceed this file size."
msgstr "BackupPlus dividirá los datos de copia de seguridad cuando los archivos superen este tamaño."

#. translators: %s: The default value of the backup split size
#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:323
#, php-format
msgid "The default value is %s megabytes."
msgstr "El valor predeterminado es %s megabytes."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:324
msgid "Be careful to leave some margin if your web-server has a hard size limit (e.g. the 2 GB / 2048 MB limit on some 32-bit servers/file systems)."
msgstr "Se cuidadoso en dejar algo de margen si tu servidor web tiene un límite de tamaño estricto (por ejemplo, el límite de 2 GB / 2048 MB en algunos servidores/sistemas de archivos de 32 bits)."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:325
msgid "The higher the value, the more server resources are required to create the archive."
msgstr "Cuanto mayor sea el valor, más recursos del servidor se requieren para crear el archivo."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:331
msgid "Delete local backup"
msgstr "Eliminar copia de seguridad local"

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:332
msgid "Check this to delete any superfluous backup files from your server after the backup run finishes (i.e. Whilst this option is unchecked, files sent to remote storage will also remain stored locally, and no locally stored files will be deleted in response to any retention rules)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:336
msgid "Backup directory"
msgstr "Directorio de respaldo"

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:346
msgid "This is where BackupPlus will write the zip files it creates initially."
msgstr "Aquí es donde BackupPlus escribirá los archivos zip que se crean inicialmente."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:346
msgid "This directory must be writable by your web server."
msgstr "Este directorio debe ser editable por tu servidor web."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:346
msgid "It is relative to your content directory (which by default is called wp-content)."
msgstr "Está relacionado a tu carpeta de contenido (que por defecto se llama wp-content)."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:346
msgid "Do not place it inside your uploads or plugins directory, as that will cause recursion (backups of backups of backups of...)."
msgstr ""

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:352
msgid "Use the server's SSL certificates"
msgstr "Usa los certificados SSL del servidor"

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:353
msgid "By default BackupPlus uses its own store of SSL certificates to verify the identity of remote sites (i.e. to make sure it is talking to the real Dropbox, Amazon S3, etc., and not an attacker)."
msgstr "Por defecto, BackupPlus utiliza su propio almacén de certificados SSL para verificar la identidad de sitios remotos (es decir, para asegurarse de que está comunicándose con el verdadero Dropbox, Amazon S3, etc., y no con un atacante)."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:353
msgid "We keep these up to date."
msgstr "Mantenemos estos actualizados."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:353
msgid "However, if you get an SSL error, then choosing this option (which causes BackupPlus to use your web server's collection instead) may help."
msgstr "Sin embargo, si obtiene un error SSL, entonces elegir esta opción (lo que hace que BackupPlus use la colección de tu servidor web en su lugar) puede ayudar."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:357
msgid "Do not verify SSL certificates"
msgstr "No verificar certificados SSL"

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:358
msgid "Choosing this option lowers your security by stopping BackupPlus from verifying the identity of encrypted sites that it connects to (e.g. Dropbox, Google Drive)."
msgstr "Elegir esta opción reduce su seguridad al impedir que BackupPlus verifique la identidad de los sitios encriptados a los que se conecta (por ejemplo, Dropbox, Google Drive)."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:358
msgid "It means that BackupPlus will be using SSL only for encryption of traffic, and not for authentication."
msgstr "Significa que BackupPlus usará SSL solo para el cifrado del tráfico, y no para la autenticación."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:358
msgid "Note that not all cloud backup methods are necessarily using SSL authentication."
msgstr "Tenga en cuenta que no todos los métodos de copia de seguridad en la nube utilizan necesariamente autenticación SSL."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:362
msgid "Disable SSL entirely where possible"
msgstr "Deshabilitar SSL por completo cuando sea posible"

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:363
msgid "Choosing this option lowers your security by stopping BackupPlus from using SSL for authentication and encrypted transport at all, where possible."
msgstr "Elegir esta opción reduce su seguridad al impedir que BackupPlus use SSL para la autenticación y todo el transporte encriptado, cuando esto sea posible."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:363
msgid "Note that some cloud storage providers do not allow this (e.g. Dropbox), so with those providers this setting will have no effect."
msgstr "Tenga en cuenta que algunos proveedores de almacenamiento en la nube no permiten esto (ejemplo: Dropbox), por lo que con estos proveedores esta configuración no tendrá efecto."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:363
msgid "For certificate errors, check that your server has an up-to-date CA certificate bundle."
msgstr ""

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:367
msgid "Automatic updates"
msgstr "Actualizaciones automáticas"

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:368
msgid "Ask WordPress to automatically update BackupPlus when it finds an available update."
msgstr "Permite que WordPress actualice BackupPlus automáticamente al detectar una actualización."

#: templates/wp-admin/settings/form-contents.php:368
msgid "Read more about Easy Updates Manager"
msgstr "Lee más sobre Easy Updates Manager"

